# Anchored to the repo root on purpose.
#
# An UNANCHORED pattern matches at ANY depth. A bare `cli` here once swallowed
# src/cli/ — the two files the registry refactor added were silently ignored,
# never committed, and CI (a fresh checkout) saw src/cli.ts importing modules
# that did not exist. It stayed red for hours, while a local checkout looked
# perfectly healthy because the files were still on disk.
#
# `bin` and `dist` are the same class of latent bug: they are safe today only
# because no nested bin/ or dist/ exists yet. Anchoring makes that explicit
# instead of accidental.
/bin/
/dist/
/cli

# Dependency and build artifacts.
node_modules/
*.log
*.backup
.fox-previous
__pycache__/
